{"name":"Tickle Me Pink","hex":"#fc89ac","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tickle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of tickling.","An itchy feeling resembling the result of tickling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch repeatedly or stroke delicately in a manner which typically causes laughter, pleasure and twitching.","To feel as if the body part in question is being tickled."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tickle"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tickle Me Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Tickle Me Pink was an American rock band from Fort Collins, Colorado, signed to Wind-Up Records. The band was made up of Sean Kennedy, Stefan Runstrom (drums), Joey Barba (guitar) and Steven Beck. After independently releasing their first two EPs, If Only We Were Twenty One and Up (2005) and Half Seas Over (2006), the band released its first album, Madeline, on July 1, 2008. The album's release coincided with the death of bassist Johnny Schou, reportedly due to a heroin overdose. Schou was replaced by Joey Barba, a longtime friend of the band."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tickle_Me_Pink"},{"title":"Tickle Me","blocks":[{"text":"Tickle Me is a 1965 American musical comedy Western film directed by Norman Taurog, written by Elwood Ullman and Edward Bernds, and starring Elvis Presley as a champion rodeo bull rider and bronco buster, with Julie Adams and Jocelyn Lane in supporting roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Ticklemeposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tickle_Me"},{"title":"Tickling","blocks":[{"text":"Tickling is the act of touching a part of a person's body in a way that causes involuntary twitching movements or laughter. The word evolved from the Middle English tikelen, perhaps frequentative of ticken, to touch lightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Zuber_Buhler_Fritz_Tickling_The_Baby.jpg/330px-Zuber_Buhler_Fritz_Tickling_The_Baby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tickling"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/James_John_Hill_%28circle%29_Being_tickled.jpg/500px-James_John_Hill_%28circle%29_Being_tickled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/James_John_Hill_%28circle%29_Being_tickled.jpg/1280px-James_John_Hill_%28circle%29_Being_tickled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/James_John_Hill_%28circle%29_Being_tickled.jpg/500px-James_John_Hill_%28circle%29_Being_tickled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"James John Hill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_John_Hill_(circle)_Being_tickled.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg/500px-Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg/1280px-Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg/500px-Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"François Boucher – Le sommeil interrompu","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFran%C3%A7ois_Boucher_-_Le_sommeil_interrompu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACherry_B